# Repository root ignores.
#
# The backend and frontend each have their own .gitignore for node_modules,
# build output and .env files. This file covers what sits at the ROOT, which
# nothing was excluding: the two directories here hold live production data,
# not source code, and publishing either one is a data breach rather than an
# untidy repository.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrets --
# Also covered per-package, repeated here so a root-level file cannot slip out.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
# The biometric gateway's config holds the shared token.
biometric-gateway/gateway.env

# ------------------------------------------------- cloud credentials (GCP) --
# Service-account key files. A committed key is a standing credential to the
# whole project that survives in history after deletion, and GitHub's secret
# scanning finds them faster than attackers only some of the time.
#
# None of these are needed for this deployment: Cloud Build and Cloud Run each
# run as their own service identity, and `gcloud auth login` uses your account.
# If a file matching these appears, something has gone wrong.
*service-account*.json
*serviceaccount*.json
*sa-key*.json
gcp-*.json
application_default_credentials.json
.gcloud/

# ------------------------------------------------- employee documents (PII) --
# Uploaded identity documents: national ID, TIN, passport and driving licence
# scans of real people, stored outside the served tree precisely because they
# must not be publicly readable. They belong on the server's disk and in
# backups, never in source control.
attachments/

# ------------------------------------------------ database dumps (PII + creds) --
# Mongo exports taken before migrations. These carry employee records, salary
# structures, payslips and audit logs -- and users.json, refreshtokens.json and
# verificationtokens.json, which hold password hashes and session tokens. A
# pushed refresh token is an account takeover, and a deleted commit does not
# un-publish it.
backups/

# ------------------------------------------------------------- dependencies --
node_modules/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- build --
dist/
dist-ssr/
build/

# -------------------------------------------------------------------- logs --
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ------------------------------------------------------------ uploads (PII) --
# Avatars and documents written by the upload middleware at runtime.
backend/uploads/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ editor --
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
